  "status": "Refused",
  "description": "Demolition of existing warehouse(B8) to provide residential dwellings (C3)",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development fails to provide sufficient justification\r\nfor the total loss of employment workspace on non-designated employment land\r\nwithout first exploring a mixed-use scheme. Therefore, the principle of\r\ndevelopment has not been established contrary to Policy 28 of the Waltham\r\nForest Local Pan Part 1 (2024).",
    "The proposed rear boundary treatment fails to sufficiently protect\r\nthe proposed dwellings from overlooking, due to the proposed boundary treatment\r\nnot being consistent with the gradient of Warley Close contrary to Policy 57 of\r\nthe Waltham Forest Local Pan Part 1 (2024).",
    "Due to the close proximity of the existing rear residential\r\nneighbouring buildings, the first and second floor bedroom windows within the\r\nproposed dwelling(s) would have a detrimental impact on&nbsp;the privacy to the\r\nresidential occupiers of Units 8 and 9 Lea Park Trading Estate contrary to Policy\r\n57 of the Waltham Forest Local Pan Part 1 (2024).",
    "Due to a lack of information relating to the non-provision of\r\nexisting and proposed streetscene elevations, the application as submitted fails\r\nto adequately demonstrate the impact of the proposed boundary treatment on entrance\r\nto the application site in relation to the existing streetscene contrary to Policy\r\n53 of the Waltham Forest Local Pan Part 1 (2024).",
    "Due to insufficient information relating to the received daylight\r\nand sunlight report not taking into consideration the impact to rooflights of buildings\r\nwithin the Lea Park Trading Estate. The application as submitted fails to\r\nadequately demonstrate that the proposed three storey buildings would not have\r\nan unreasonable amenity impact to all of the rear buildings contrary to Policy 57\r\nof the Waltham Forest Local Pan Part 1 (2024).",
    "No justification has been provided regarding the proposed\r\ndeparture from the housing mix requirements of the Local Planning Authority,\r\ncontrary to Policy 15 of the Waltham Forest Local Pan Part 1 (2024).",
    "In the absence of a satisfactory Outline Construction\r\nLogistic Plan, a full assessment&nbsp;of how the proposed development would be\r\nbuilt or serviced without severely affecting the public highway could not be\r\nmade in accordance with Policies T7 of the London Plan (2021) and Policy 65 of\r\nthe Waltham Forest Local Pan Part 1 (2024).",
    "The application as submitted,&nbsp;comprises of inconsistent\r\ninformation. The proposed &#39;typical ground floor layout&#39; plan&nbsp;illustrates\r\nprovision for 2No. secure cycle stores within the rear garden of each property.\r\nWhereas the Planning and Transport Statement(s) make reference to the site\r\nhaving&nbsp;3 long-term and 2 short-term spaces. The application as submitted therefore\r\nfails to adequately demonstrate that there would be sufficient secure parking\r\nstorage contrary to Appendix 1 - Parking Standards and Policy 61 of the Waltham\r\nForest Local Pan Part 1 (2024).",
    "The furthest proposed dwellinghouses houses from the main entrance\r\nexceeds a 60m walking distance from the communal refuse and recycling\r\nstorage, this is contrary to the Waste &amp; Recycling Policy for Developers\r\n(2022).",
    "The applicant has failed to provide information of how the communal\r\nrefuse and recycling area/ bins would be accessed/ operated by somebody with a disability,\r\nthis is contrary to the Waste &amp; Recycling Policy for Developers (2022).",
    "The applicant has failed to enter into a S106 agreement and\r\ntherefore not in compliance with Policy 94 of the Waltham Forest Local Plan\r\nPart 1 (2024) and the Waltham Forest Supplementary Planning Document “Planning\r\nObligations” SPD, specifically in relation to the following planning\r\nobligations requirements (figures applicable at the time of the assessment of\r\nthe application):A) Highways and\r\nTransportation:&nbsp;i) Car Free Development - the\r\n      development is to be classified as car-free and residents will not be\r\n      eligible for parking permits.ii) A condition survey is required of\r\n      the carriageway and footways fronting the site prior to the commencement\r\n      of any works.iii)&nbsp;A S106 request of\r\n      £9,000&nbsp;is requested toward improving sustainable modes of transport\r\n      including walking and cycling in the sites vicinity which will directly\r\n      benefit new residents in this development.iv) A&nbsp;S106 contribution of\r\n      £750&nbsp;is requested for CLP monitoring.v) S278 works –The extent of the works will include\r\n       but are not limited to:Renewal of the footway along the\r\n       frontage of the site.Renewal of the access and road\r\n       markings along the frontage of the site.B) SAMMS:i)\r\n      SAMMS - A financial contribution of £5,850.00 towards Strategic Access\r\n      Management and Monitoring measures (SAMMs).C) Carbon offset:Carbon\r\n      Offset Fund (COF) contributions will be required for any shortfall in\r\n      emission reductions, calculated to be £11,778.00D) Legal Fees:i)\r\n      Payment of the Council’s legal fees for the preparation and completion of\r\n      the Legal Agreement.ii)\r\n      Monitoring Fee - A financial contribution towards the implementation and\r\n      monitoring of and securing compliance with the S106, equal to 5% of the\r\n      total of all other financial contributions .\r\n"
  ],
